**Project:** ZDX Muse Synthesis
**Purpose:** Meta AI hackathon entry and production\-oriented data intelligence platform
**Owner:** ZeroDriveX
**Revision:** 2026\-10\-27 — integrated real\-data\-first policy
**Target:** New, independently deployable application, architecturally informed by ZDX Data Synthesis

> **Instructions to Muse Code:** Treat this document as the authoritative implementation brief. Implement incrementally, verify all provider assumptions against official current Meta documentation and live account access, and keep the existing ZDX Data Synthesis production environment untouched. Do not fabricate completed work, provider capabilities, metrics, or test outcomes.

## 0\. Mission and non\-negotiable boundaries

Build **ZDX Muse Synthesis**, a state\-of\-the\-art, real\-data\-first platform for ingesting, understanding, transforming, validating, enriching, and packaging authentic data, with tightly controlled AI\-generated augmentation\. Reproduce the useful capabilities of the existing ZeroDriveX Data Synthesis platform and substantially improve durability, scalability, commercial value, quality measurement, lineage, UX, and autonomous processing\.

This is **not** an unrestricted fictional\-record generator\. For datasets designated for model training, the platform must enforce a **maximum 30% synthetic contribution in the final exported dataset**, with **at least 70% provenance\-verifiable authentic source data**\. This is a product policy rather than a universal scientific guarantee against model collapse\. Never claim the threshold itself prevents model collapse; assess quality, distribution drift, leakage, contamination, and downstream evaluation independently\.

Use **Meta Muse models for all generative and semantic AI operations**\. Use **Muse Code as the principal coding agent** to develop the new project\. Conventional deterministic code must handle arithmetic, ingestion, parsing, schema validation, authorization, job orchestration, lineage, budgeting, statistics, and persistence\. No OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Groq, OpenRouter, Nebius, Ollama, or other non\-Meta inference backends in operational AI workflows\.

Build in a separate repository &#40;suggested name `zdx-muse-synthesis`&#41;, with isolated database, credentials, storage, and deployment\. **Do not modify the existing ZDX Data Synthesis production system\.** Treat the existing app as a read\-only design/functional reference where the hackathon rules permit; document any reused code\. Before copying source, verify the hackathon’s eligibility requirements for pre\-existing work, permitted SDKs, required model use, and submission evidence\.

Do not use Vercel; prefer existing authorized ZDX infrastructure with a minimal, standalone Docker deployment\. Do not connect to the existing ZDX inference pool or agent memory pool\. Avoid new infrastructure that a solo operator cannot maintain\.

